			],
			"Message": "docs(Common): Restyle README with condensed sections, component table, and funding badges\n\nCompact the Common crate README by removing the header HTML table, the full directory tree listing, lengthy per-section explanations, and the verbose funding acknowledgements block. Replace with a tighter narrative structure: add an emoji-accented title, an inline Overview paragraph summarizing all core concepts, a new Key Components table linking each service domain to its source path, an Architecture Principles table, and a compact In the Land Project section. Simplify the See Also section into Related Documentation preserving all essential links. Replace the License and Changelog sections with inline references. Move the ActionEffect code example after the architecture principles, keeping the Getting Started guide intact.\n\nThe restyled README is scannable at a glance, surfaces the project structure table, and eliminates redundant whitespace and decorative elements while preserving all technical content.",
			"SHA": "bc87a0d731c20330b6213f5c790c168b304c5ba4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-11T23:28:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				365,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Common): Add extension management, output, process, search, and language IPC channels\n\nExtend the IPC channel registry with nine new channel definitions across multiple domains to support richer frontend-backend communication:\n\n- Extensions: `ExtensionsDownload`, `ExtensionsGetCoreTranslation`, `ExtensionsSearch` for extension lifecycle and metadata retrieval\n- Output: `OutputDispose`, `OutputReplace` for managing output panel lifecycle\n- Process: `ProcessGetMemoryInfo` for runtime memory inspection\n- Search: `SearchCancel`, `SearchClearCache` for search session management\n- Languages: `LanguagesGetLanguages` for language enumeration\n\nAll additions are purely additive to the `DefineChannels!` macro with no breaking changes to existing channels.",
			"SHA": "8eb7670871fa77578f75310b38ce325d624af124"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-11T21:58:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				365,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Common): Add keybinding evaluation and resolution IPC channels\n\nIntroduce two new IPC channel definitions in the Common crate's channel registry:\n- `KeybindingEvaluateWhen` for evaluating keybinding when-clauses\n- `KeybindingResolve` for resolving keybinding conflicts and priorities\n\nThese channels extend the keybinding management IPC surface to support dynamic when-clause evaluation and conflict resolution, enabling more sophisticated keybinding behavior in the editor frontend. The changes are purely additive to the channel definition macro with no breaking modifications to existing channels.",
			"SHA": "d3931720d0ed4fa1a959281d5009488e4c80374d"
		},
